        "original_id": "a78fc134-a495-5583-8877-de9687d032ad",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Independent Commission on the Voting System, Jenkins Commission\n- People: Roy Jenkins\n- Products: Alternative Vote Plus (AV+)\n- Places: United Kingdom\n- Topics: electoral system reform\n\nFacts:\n- Roy Jenkins was born on 11 November 1920 and died on 5 January 2003.\n- Roy Jenkins was a British Labour Party, SDP, and Liberal Democrat politician and a biographer of British political leaders.\n- The Independent Commission on the Voting System was popularly known as the Jenkins Commission after its chairman Roy Jenkins.\n- The Jenkins Commission examined possible reform of the United Kingdom electoral system.\n- In 1998, the Jenkins Commission devised Alternative Vote Plus.\n- The Jenkins Commission first proposed Alternative Vote Plus as a system for elections to the Parliament of the United Kingdom.",
